1
00:00:16,410 --> 00:00:45,993
Do you like the dress?

2
00:00:45,993 --> 00:00:46,987
I love it.

3
00:00:46,987 --> 00:00:48,647
I designed it myself.

4
00:00:48,647 --> 00:00:50,625
It's beautiful.

5
00:00:50,625 --> 00:00:52,825
Are you ready?

6
00:00:52,825 --> 00:00:54,357
We're supposed to be there

7
00:00:54,357 --> 00:00:55,363
before the guests arrive.

8
00:00:55,363 --> 00:00:56,581
I know. I know.

9
00:00:56,581 --> 00:01:02,937
Help me with this tie, will you?

10
00:01:02,937 --> 00:01:05,944
Honey, I'm scared to death.

11
00:01:05,944 --> 00:01:09,710
But this is what you've been working for all these years.

12
00:01:09,710 --> 00:01:10,196
No, no.

13
00:01:10,196 --> 00:01:12,671
I worked to put together a book of photographs.

14
00:01:12,671 --> 00:01:13,871
This is show business.

15
00:01:13,871 --> 00:01:16,085
Well, it's all part of the same job.

16
00:01:16,085 --> 00:01:17,427
Just relax and enjoy it.

17
00:01:17,427 --> 00:01:20,405
You're right.

18
00:01:20,405 --> 00:01:29,339
I earned this, and I'm going to enjoy it.

19
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:32,317
As soon as I recover from my nervous breakdown.

20
00:01:32,317 --> 00:01:37,279
What are you afraid of?

21
00:01:37,279 --> 00:01:38,271
Everything.

22
00:01:38,271 --> 00:01:40,193
A critic was there this morning.

23
00:01:40,193 --> 00:01:41,251
He probably hates my work.

24
00:01:41,251 --> 00:01:43,545
I have to sign copies of my book for a lot of people

25
00:01:43,545 --> 00:01:44,229
I never met before.

26
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:46,080
My new shoes hurt my feet ...

27
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:57,569
You're going to be a great success.

28
00:01:57,569 --> 00:02:00,118
Are you ready?

29
00:02:00,118 --> 00:02:04,581
As soon as I get these cuff links on.

30
00:02:04,581 --> 00:02:08,652
Let me help.

31
00:02:08,652 --> 00:02:16,986
Mom and Dad are already on their way down to the gallery.

32
00:02:16,986 --> 00:02:20,584
There! You look very attractive.

33
00:02:20,584 --> 00:02:23,317
Thank you.

34
00:02:23,317 --> 00:02:26,587
Well, I suppose I've run out of excuses.

35
00:02:26,587 --> 00:02:30,898
Mm-hmm. Let's go ...

36
00:02:30,898 --> 00:02:31,876
Oh, one minute.

37
00:02:31,876 --> 00:02:35,854
Before we go to the gallery,

38
00:02:35,854 --> 00:02:37,054
I just want to tell you

39
00:02:37,054 --> 00:02:38,984
that I never could have done this book

40
00:02:38,984 --> 00:02:40,810
without your help and your love.

41
00:02:40,810 --> 00:02:43,788
I appreciate it.

42
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:46,766
Thanks.

43
00:02:46,766 --> 00:02:58,678
Now, no more stalling.

44
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:01,656
What is it?

45
00:03:01,656 --> 00:03:03,656
There's nobody here!

46
00:03:03,656 --> 00:03:05,107
Of course not, Richard.

47
00:03:05,107 --> 00:03:10,589
Your show doesn't begin until eight thirty.

48
00:03:10,589 --> 00:03:13,567
Oh. Right.

49
00:03:13,567 --> 00:03:17,045
Richard! Welcome! Good luck tonight! Richard

50
00:03:17,045 --> 00:03:17,878
Well, thanks.

51
00:03:17,878 --> 00:03:19,776
This is my publisher, Harvey Carlson.

52
00:03:19,776 --> 00:03:21,703
You've met my wife Marilyn ...

53
00:03:21,703 --> 00:03:22,501
Charmed.

54
00:03:22,501 --> 00:03:24,448
My mother, Ellen Stewart.

55
00:03:24,448 --> 00:03:25,479
Harvey Carlson.

56
00:03:25,479 --> 00:03:27,159
It's good to meet you.

57
00:03:27,159 --> 00:03:28,957
This is my father, Dr. Philip Stewart ...

58
00:03:28,957 --> 00:03:30,290
Nice to meet you, Mr. Carlson.

59
00:03:30,290 --> 00:03:31,717
My brother Robbie ...

60
00:03:31,717 --> 00:03:31,917
Hi.

61
00:03:31,717 --> 00:03:31,935
Hi.

62
00:03:31,935 --> 00:03:36,413
And this is my sister Susan and her husband Harry Bennett

63
00:03:36,413 --> 00:03:38,144
and his daughter Michelle.

64
00:03:38,144 --> 00:03:40,369
It's nice to meet you.

65
00:03:40,369 --> 00:03:44,347
And this gentleman is my grandfather, Malcolm Stewart.

66
00:03:44,347 --> 00:03:46,325
Welcome, Mr. Stewart.

67
00:03:46,325 --> 00:03:48,325
Well, make yourselves comfortable.

68
00:03:48,325 --> 00:03:51,639
There are hors d'oeuvres at the table, fruit punch at the bar.

69
00:03:51,639 --> 00:03:52,281
Help yourselves.

70
00:03:52,281 --> 00:03:55,259
Can I get you something, Mr. Stewart?

71
00:03:55,259 --> 00:03:56,599
No, thank you.

72
00:03:56,599 --> 00:04:00,357
You can feel very proud of your grandson, Mr. Stewart.

73
00:04:00,357 --> 00:04:01,215
I do.

74
00:04:01,215 --> 00:04:04,193
I'm proud of all my grandchildren, Mr. Carlson.

75
00:04:04,193 --> 00:04:05,360
Of course.

76
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:06,193
Feel free to look around.

77
00:04:06,193 --> 00:04:08,691
If you need anything, just ask.

78
00:04:08,691 --> 00:04:10,149
Thank you.

79
00:04:10,149 --> 00:04:12,149
Harvey? Harvey

80
00:04:12,149 --> 00:04:12,816
Yes?

81
00:04:12,816 --> 00:04:17,569
Did Mitchell Johnson's review come out yet? Mitchell Johnsson

82
00:04:17,569 --> 00:04:18,545
Not yet.

83
00:04:18,545 --> 00:04:56,570
The newspapers don't come out till about ten o'clock.

84
00:04:56,570 --> 00:05:09,708
When they come out, we'll get it.

85
00:05:09,708 --> 00:05:10,163
Thanks.

86
00:05:10,163 --> 00:05:10,617
Ready?

87
00:05:10,617 --> 00:05:13,799
Yes. Have the people arrived?

88
00:05:13,799 --> 00:05:14,686
The guests are waiting.

89
00:05:14,686 --> 00:05:25,736
Tom's about to open the doors. Tom

90
00:05:25,736 --> 00:05:30,887
Good luck! And stop worrying!

91
00:05:30,887 --> 00:05:33,887
They're going to love it.
